url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma","html_url":"https://github.com/Jisse-Meruma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T09:42:47Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T09:42:47Z","body":"Hi @kradalby, Would it be possible to continue the discussion of this PR?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2690188750/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2690520911","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2302#issuecomment-2690520911","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2302","id":2690520911,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886gXhdP","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T12:25:49Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T12:25:49Z","body":"Sorry, I have been swamped, I've read up a bit this morning and this is my thoughts:\r\n\r\nI think these headers should be limited to the api, that covers the main use case of allowing CORS for the different WebUIs. I do not think we should add it to all the other endpoints, that is quite an exotic use case and while I agree with @routerino that it is bad UX to ask people using the API and WebUI to setup a proxy to have CORS, I do think that this is exotic enough to say that you need to do it in a proxy.\r\n\r\nI do not really want to support `*`, so setting a domain would be required. From what I understand from the spec, you can only have a single origin, not a list, so we should allow the list of a single domain (I might be wrong about this one, please enlighten me).\r\nE.g. headscale server is: myheadscale.net and ui is: admin.myheadscale.net\r\n\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2690520911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2697062148","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2302#issuecomment-2697062148","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2302","id":2697062148,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886gwecE","user":{"login":"Jisse-Meruma","id":95289996,"node_id":"U_kgDOBa4CjA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95289996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma","html_url":"https://github.com/Jisse-Meruma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T10:50:09Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T10:50:09Z","body":"\r\nHi @kradalby,\r\n\r\nAs of writing, the current commit no longer supports the use of `*` for the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header, as it could pose a security risk. You can now only set a specific origin. However, considering that multiple clients might connect to the server, I have implemented the flexibility to specify multiple origins.\r\n\r\nThe code loops through the list of allowed origins and checks if the request origin is in the list. If it is, the corresponding header is added to enable Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) for that specific origin. This technique is a standard approach when dealing with a list of Allowed origins, as documented here: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Access-Control-Allow-Origin.\r\n\r\nI understand your concerns about enabling CORS on sensitive routes and the potential security risks involved. Given that we no longer allow the use of `*` for the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header, administrators can now specify only particular URLs to permit connections to Headscale via the web.\r\n\r\nEven if a rouge website was allowed to communicate with Headscale through the web, it would still require to go to the mandatory security layers to fully register a node. Additionally, Tailscale is beginning to implement web clients that can already connect to the official control server with CORS enabled.\r\n\r\nTo add an extra layer of security, we can consider allowing CORS on sensitive endpoints only for origins that use the HTTPS protocol. This ensures that the data is transmitted securely and reduces the risk associated with allowing CORS on less secure origins.\r\n\r\nHowever, if this approach is not preferred, I am more than willing to make adjustments to enable CORS only for the WEBUI API.\r\n\r\nThank you for your understanding and please let me know if you have any further suggestions or concerns.\r\nBest regards,\r\nJisse Meruma\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2697062148/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2747622148","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2302#issuecomment-2747622148","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2302","id":2747622148,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886jxWME","user":{"login":"Jisse-Meruma","id":95289996,"node_id":"U_kgDOBa4CjA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95289996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma","html_url":"https://github.com/Jisse-Meruma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jisse-Meruma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T10:27:00Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T10:27:00Z","body":"Hi @kradalby, I know you are quite busy. But still I would like to know if there is a change we could move this forward. I would like to know your opinion of my latest suggestion so that I can make a code draft for you.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2747622148/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2827773799","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2302#issuecomment-2827773799","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2302","id":2827773799,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886ojGdn","user":{"login":"scarytom","id":15207,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15207?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scarytom","html_url":"https://github.com/scarytom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scarytom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scarytom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scarytom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scarytom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com